{"cluster_id": "C-2918", "topic": "CachedPartFolderAccess::publishEntries performs startBuild, adoptEvidence for every", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B008-027", "B008-078"], "canonical_claim": "`CachedPartFolderAccess::publishEntries` performs `startBuild`, `adoptEvidence` for every entry, `stageManifest`, `precommitAdd`, and `promoteBuild` as the shared committed-publish sequence.; `publishEntries` is the shared sequence `startBuild -> adoptEvidence per entry -> stageManifest -> precommitAdd -> promoteBuild`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-08-cas-part-folder-cache-phase2.md#task-5", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-08-cas-part-folder-cache-design.md#two-level-api"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2919", "topic": "republishRef moves a committed source by", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B008-028"], "canonical_claim": "`republishRef` moves a committed source by publishing a fresh destination manifest and then dropping the source; an absent source returns `false` without writing.", "issue_ids": ["rev.15"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-08-cas-part-folder-cache-phase2.md#task-5"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2920", "topic": "dropNamespace removes retained views whose canonical", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B008-046"], "canonical_claim": "`dropNamespace` removes retained views whose canonical cache keys start with the namespace plus the NUL separator and increments the invalidation metric.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-08-cas-part-folder-cache-phase4.md#task-2"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2921", "topic": "The facade's committed-ref write API includes", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B008-069"], "canonical_claim": "The facade's committed-ref write API includes `promoteBuild`, `publishEntries`, `republishRef`, `updateMutableFiles`, `dropRef`, `dropRefIfPresent`, `dropRefBestEffort`, and `dropNamespace`; pass-through operations such as `listRefs`, `listNamespaces`, `listMirroredChildren`, namespace files, mountpoint objects, and `locate` remain on `Cas::Store`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-08-cas-part-folder-cache-design.md#cachedpartfolderaccess"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2922", "topic": "The in-flight transaction overlay remains above", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B008-076"], "canonical_claim": "The in-flight transaction overlay remains above the facade; committed-source `createHardLink` and `moveFile` use `ForceFresh` access, while in-flight overlay reads may continue to use raw read-only `locate` calls.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-08-cas-part-folder-cache-design.md#method-routing"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2923", "topic": "Each level-1 facade mutation performs its", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B008-077"], "canonical_claim": "Each level-1 facade mutation performs its underlying store or build operation and erases affected retained views only after success, except `dropRefBestEffort`, which erases even after swallowing a failure.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-08-cas-part-folder-cache-design.md#two-level-api"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2924", "topic": "Birth-completion is allowed only from an", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B010-008"], "canonical_claim": "Birth-completion is allowed only from an absent meta, representing a crashed pre-meta birth; it is never allowed from a `tombstone` meta.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-10-cas-meta-descriptor-raw-body.md#L19-L36"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2925", "topic": "A condemned object is contract", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B010-013", "B011-037", "B011-039"], "canonical_claim": "A condemned object is never read or fetched to revive it; revival uses a fresh upload or recreation from source, except for the documented `INV-1` tokenless copy-forward of a committed-source dependency whose condemned body is still present. Only a writer that has displaced the body with a fresh incarnation token may publish `Clean`, through `uploadFromSource` with `writeResurrectMetaClean` or tokenless committed-source `copyForwardFromCondemned`. A spared hash may remain `Condemned` indefinitely; normal reads do not consult the marker, and the next `putBlob` must materialize or copy-forward a fresh incarnation before publishing `Clean`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-10-cas-meta-descriptor-raw-body.md#L38-L52", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-11-cas-deposed-leader-clearsparedmeta-fix-design.md#fix", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-11-cas-deposed-leader-clearsparedmeta-fix-design.md#interactions"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2926", "topic": "The writer's meta state machine adopts", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B010-024"], "canonical_claim": "The writer's meta state machine adopts a clean meta without a body `HEAD`, resurrects a condemned meta with `casMeta` and no body re-upload, and handles an absent meta by re-establishing the raw body from its own source before creating clean meta.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-10-cas-meta-descriptor-raw-body.md#L824-L1155"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2927", "topic": "A writer observing a tombstone waits", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B010-025"], "canonical_claim": "A writer observing a tombstone waits through bounded fresh meta reads and then retries fresh upload after the meta becomes absent; if the bound is exhausted, `putBlob` throws `ABORTED` and never changes the tombstone to clean.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-10-cas-meta-descriptor-raw-body.md#L824-L1155"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2928", "topic": "Promote skips meta revalidation for tokened", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B010-027"], "canonical_claim": "Promote skips meta revalidation for tokened leaves; for a non-tokened leaf it fails with `ABORTED` on absent meta, accepts clean meta, and copy-forwards only a condemned meta by CASing it to clean.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-10-cas-meta-descriptor-raw-body.md#L1156-L1291"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2929", "topic": "copyForwardFromCondemned is a pure meta CAS", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B010-028"], "canonical_claim": "`copyForwardFromCondemned` is a pure meta CAS for a condemned raw-body leaf and performs no body GET or PUT; tombstone or absent meta is fail-closed because the tokenless promote path has no source.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-10-cas-meta-descriptor-raw-body.md#L1156-L1291"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2930", "topic": "A condemned row subsumes contract", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B011-008", "B011-022"], "canonical_claim": "A condemned row subsumes the zero marker, while a plain `kZeroMarker` is emitted only when the object is absent at condemnation and remains transient for the generation. Fresh zero transitions mint a `kCondemned` row from the `head_blob` observation; an absent object produces only a plain `kZeroMarker`, and clamp suppression carries pending rows unchanged while keeping floor-passed rows condemned-only.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-10-cas-retired-in-snapshot-design.md#merge", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-10-cas-retired-in-snapshot-design.md#run-rows"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2931", "topic": "A blob's (algo, digest) identity is", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B011-045"], "canonical_claim": "A blob's `(algo, digest)` identity is immutable from upload through exact-token deletion, so changing the configured write algorithm does not rehash an existing blob.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-11-cas-mixed-algo-pools-design.md#real-invariant"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2932", "topic": "Deduplication is keyed by BlobRef and", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B011-060"], "canonical_claim": "Deduplication is keyed by `BlobRef` and therefore works only within one algorithm subset; equal content written under different algorithms naturally has different keys and does not cross-deduplicate.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-11-cas-mixed-algo-pools-design.md#consumers"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2933", "topic": "The S3 staging lifecycle contract", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B011-132", "B011-135", "B011-156"], "canonical_claim": "The S3 staging lifecycle is `precommitAdd(edge) \u2192 stage \u2192 promote(copy)+condemn-check \u2192 delete staging \u2192 promoteBuild(visible)`; a manifest cannot become visible before the blob exists at its content key. A staging object is deleted only after promotion and the condemn check complete, because it remains the resurrection source during that gate. For S3 staging, `publishStaging` must run the same `putBlob` condemn/resurrect gate as local staging; the only changed upload primitive is conditional server-side copy from the staging object.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-11-cas-s3-native-staging.md#task-5", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-11-cas-s3-native-staging-design.md#lifecycle"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2934", "topic": "On a successful conditional copy, the", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B011-133"], "canonical_claim": "On a successful conditional copy, the destination ETag from `CopyObject` or `CompleteMultipartUpload` becomes the blob incarnation token; on `PreconditionFailed`, the writer HEADs the destination and executes the existing condemn/resurrect gate.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-11-cas-s3-native-staging-design.md#lifecycle"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2935", "topic": "A failed current-writer build removes its", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B012-037"], "canonical_claim": "A failed current-writer build removes its exact precommit before retirement; a fenced successor removes predecessor-epoch precommits in bounded batches after recovery.", "issue_ids": ["rev.4"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-12-cas-ref-table-snapshot-log-phase1.md#L331-L334"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2936", "topic": "Manifest-trust relink adoption relies on the", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B014-039"], "canonical_claim": "Manifest-trust relink adoption relies on the source pinning the part for the whole download and the fetcher's durable precommit edge being established before adoption; trusted adoption uses `reason=\"manifest-trust\"`, an empty token, and the `CasBlobAdoptTrusted` counter without changing manifest format.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-13-cas-memory-s3-budget-optimizations-design.md#s4-relink-trust"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2937", "topic": "Decommission order is gate and claim", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B014-055"], "canonical_claim": "Decommission order is gate and claim, namespace enumeration, per-namespace ref removal, manifest-debris drain, staging sweep, roots sweep, and slot retirement strictly last; namespace removal emits ordinary negative edge deltas and does not make `GC` invent ref transitions.", "issue_ids": ["B200"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-13-cas-pool-member-decommission-design.md#core"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2938", "topic": "Recovery seals apply to Live-lifecycle tables", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B015-022"], "canonical_claim": "Recovery seals apply to `Live`-lifecycle tables, while `Removed` recoveries are not sealed and rely on ordinary namespace cleanup for late rebirth debris.", "issue_ids": ["T11"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-13-cas-ref-lease-exclusivity-rev6-design.md#seal-id"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2939", "topic": "RemovePart generated zero S3 requests in", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B015-042"], "canonical_claim": "`RemovePart` generated zero S3 requests in the soak because removal is a batched ref operation and physical deletion is deferred to GC.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-13-cas-soak-metrics-audit.md#part-log"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2940", "topic": "adoptEvidence records a tokenless, bodyless, edgeless", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B015-066"], "canonical_claim": "`adoptEvidence` records a tokenless, bodyless, edgeless dependency during the transaction body, while the destination's durable `precommitAdd` edge is appended only at commit.", "issue_ids": ["#42"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-14-cas-adoptevidence-relink-lifecycle-exposure.md#the-two-dep-recording-moments-and-the-durable-edge-timeline-grounded"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2941", "topic": "A committed-source adopt is not a", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B015-067"], "canonical_claim": "A committed-source adopt is not a pending blob, so it is never uploaded by `putBlob`; before `precommitAdd`, the destination contributes no durable in-degree edge to the adopted blob.", "issue_ids": ["#42"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-14-cas-adoptevidence-relink-lifecycle-exposure.md#the-two-dep-recording-moments-and-the-durable-edge-timeline-grounded"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2942", "topic": "grabOldParts removes a CA part only", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B015-072"], "canonical_claim": "`grabOldParts` removes a CA part only when it is `Outdated` and its `DataPartPtr` is uniquely owned.", "issue_ids": ["#42"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-14-cas-adoptevidence-relink-lifecycle-exposure.md#sub-q1-enumerate-createhardlinkadoptevidence-callers-and-whether-the-source-is-pinned"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2943", "topic": "A CA MVCC store event is", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B015-086"], "canonical_claim": "A CA MVCC store event is intended to produce one manifest repoint, and `txn_version.txt.tmp` is never created on CA.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-14-cas-all-tree-part-files-design.md#mvcc-short-circuit-and-the-eager-hook-deletion"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2944", "topic": "A committed-file unlink stages contract", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B015-087", "B016-015", "B051-055"], "canonical_claim": "A committed-file unlink stages a removal mark; if the whole part is also removed, the mark is superseded and the normal ref-drop path pays zero repoints. For a committed content-file unlink, `unlinkFile` stages the path in `st.content_removed`; publishing filters that path from carried-forward entries and repoints unless the same transaction drops the whole part ref, which supersedes and discards the marks.; CAS unlink operations were eagerly staged in memory and program order to fix the `01603` column-TTL ordering inversion; under the two-domain invariant, unlink dispatch remains eager while the durable delete is materialized as an intent at commit.", "issue_ids": ["B123"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/upstream-patch-inventory.md#disk-object-storage-transaction-cpp", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-15-cas-all-tree-part-files.md#task-8", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-14-cas-all-tree-part-files-design.md#removal-semantics"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2945", "topic": "When publishStaging receives staged entries for", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B016-011"], "canonical_claim": "When `publishStaging` receives staged entries for an already committed ref, it force-freshly reads the current manifest, drops entries whose paths are overwritten, carries forward all other entries, appends the staged entries, uploads pending blobs, and publishes once through the repoint path.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-15-cas-all-tree-part-files.md#task-4"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2946", "topic": "Every CA disk transaction mutation updates", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B017-112"], "canonical_claim": "Every CA disk transaction mutation updates one transaction-private overlay at call time, and the existing disk `commit` is the only operation that publishes the overlay into the durable CAS namespace.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-15-cas-txn-one-pipeline-design.md#cas-txn-one-pipeline-design"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2947", "topic": "The transaction states are Open, Committed", "target": "architecture/part-lifecycle", "member_ids": ["B017-114"], "canonical_claim": "The transaction states are `Open`, `Committed`, and `Aborted`; in `Open`, writes, creates, hardlinks, deletes, moves, directory moves, and ref moves update the overlay immediately without publishing live refs.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-15-cas-txn-one-pipeline-design.md#transaction-model"]}

